WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.266
Now try the decoder.

2
00:00:01.266 --> 00:00:03.860
C V A six is the compact repository name.

3
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:13.162
C V sixty four A six zero follows the current CVA6 part-number example: family, instruction length, class, pipeline stages, and product identifier.

4
00:00:13.162 --> 00:00:21.451
C V thirty two E four zero P comes from a broader historical syntax with family, word length, class, identity, and modifier fields.

5
00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:24.994
The important habit is to stop where the evidence stops.

6
00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:31.575
A suffix can distinguish a product, but its behavior belongs in the current configuration documentation.

